From 720a487d4afadca14a84bbecedb39f8054ad0332 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: khj1222 <39723594+khj1222@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:11:02 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ink_detection threshold: add the quantile rule (apply --rule
 quantile)

calibrate also stores the median fraction of the sheet (non-zero prediction
pixels) that each labelled prediction's optimum marks, and its per-scroll check
now reports the value rule, the quantile rule and 128 side by side. apply
--rule quantile cuts a new prediction where it marks that fraction of its own
sheet, which follows a checkpoint whose scale shifts between scrolls. The value
rule stays the default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
